 "scenes": [
  {
   "id": "intro",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Tomasulo's machine can look far ahead, but only if it knows where the program is going. Every branch is a fork. Dynamic predictors learn each branch's habits while the program runs."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "head"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Dynamic branch prediction, part 1"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Here are the seven stages."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "stages"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Why predict at run time, the branch history table, and the 1-bit and 2-bit predictors."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[0..=3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Then a trace of both on a loop, the branch target buffer, and an exam question."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[4..=6]"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "why",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 1: three reasons static prediction is not enough."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 1 of 7: why predict while running"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "stages"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "why"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A branch's behaviour depends on the data. A fixed guess cannot follow a branch that changes its mind."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Deep pipelines that issue several instructions per cycle throw away a lot of work on every wrong guess."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And dynamic scheduling only helps if instructions keep flowing past branches."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "the deeper and wider the machine, the more prediction matters"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "bht",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 2: the simplest dynamic predictor is a branch history table, or branch prediction buffer. A small memory, indexed by the low bits of the branch's address."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 2 of 7: the branch history table"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "why"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "bht"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "bhm"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "bhm[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Each entry holds a prediction. In the fetch stage the hardware reads the entry for this branch, and guesses."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "bht[0..=3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "With 4096 entries, the index needs 12 bits. Instructions are 4 bytes, so the lowest 2 address bits are always zero: the index is PC bits 13 down to 2."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "bhm[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "bhm[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "There is no tag. Two branches whose addresses share those bits share an entry, and may spoil each other's prediction. That is called aliasing; with a few thousand entries it is rare."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "bhm[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "bhm[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "With 2 bits per entry, 4096 entries cost just 1 kilobyte."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "bhm[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "bhm[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "BHT: indexed by low PC bits · no tag · tiny"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "onebit",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 3: the 1-bit predictor. Each entry remembers what the branch did last time, and predicts the same again."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 3 of 7: the 1-bit predictor"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "bht"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "bhm"
      },
      {
